en.description:
The gathering, entitled “Reading Aloud for the Holidays,” will take place at the Sołacki Salon. It’s an invitation to everyone who would like to pause for a moment amid the pre-holiday bustle, listen to beautiful stories, and feel the atmosphere of the upcoming holidays.

Program:
• a group reading of Christmas Eve stories by Aneta Grabowska;
• a presentation of atmospheric works and poems prepared by participants who wish to take part;
• coffee, tea, and something sweet in a warm, festive atmosphere;
• an artistic touch: participants will have the opportunity to enrich the gathering with singing or music.

The gathering will be hosted by Anna Ciorga, who creates intimate events where books become a starting point for conversation, getting to know one another, and building relationships between generations.

Where: Sołacki Salon, 43 Wojska Polskiego Street
Time: 17:00

